#103      read  0x08 = 0x00000078
#104      write 0x08 = 0x0000000a
#105-#133  poll 0x20 x29: 0x00000001 ... 0x00000000
#134      read  0x08 = 0x00375f00
#135      write 0x60 = 0x00000042
#136      read  0x24 = 0x00000042
#137      write 0x64 = 0x00000042
#138      read  0x24 = 0x00000000
#139-#202  read-only scan of offsets 0x00-0xfc (64 reads)
== 2. per register ==
0x00  reads 3, writes 0, always reads 0x010000ed
0x04  reads 3, writes 1, 2 distinct values read; read after write = inverse of the value written (1x)
0x08  reads 4, writes 2, 3 distinct values read; read after write = a different value (2x)
0x20  reads 65, writes 0, 2 distinct values read; changed between two reads with no write in between (4x)
0x24  reads 4, writes 0, 2 distinct values read; changed between two reads with no write in between (2x)
0x60  reads 2, writes 1, always reads 0xffffffff; read after write = a different value (1x)
0x64  reads 2, writes 1, always reads 0xffffffff; read after write = a different value (1x)
0x80  reads 2, writes 0, always reads 0x00000000
0x88  reads 2, writes 0, always reads 0x00000000
0x90  reads 2, writes 0, always reads 0x00000000
0x98  reads 2, writes 0, always reads 0x00000000
offsets that only ever read 0xffffffff: 0x0c 0x10 0x14 0x18 0x1c 0x28 0x2c 0x30 0x34 0x38 0x3c 0x40 0x44 0x48 0x4c 0x50 0x54 0x58 0x5c 0x68 0x6c 0x70 0x74 0x78 0x7c 0x84 0x8c 0x94 0x9c 0xa0 0xa4 0xa8 0xac 0xb0 0xb4 0xb8 0xbc 0xc0 0xc4 0xc8 0xcc 0xd0 0xd4 0xd8 0xdc 0xe0 0xe4 0xe8 0xec 0xf0 0xf4 0xf8 0xfc
== 3. cross effects (a write, then another offset reads differently than before) ==
#68 write 0x08 = 0x00000005  ->  #69 0x20 now reads 0x00000001 (was 0x00000000)
#104 write 0x08 = 0x0000000a  ->  #105 0x20 now reads 0x00000001 (was 0x00000000)
#135 write 0x60 = 0x00000042  ->  #136 0x24 now reads 0x00000042 (was 0x00000000)
#137 write 0x64 = 0x00000042  ->  #138 0x24 now reads 0x00000000 (was 0x00000042)
